---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Passwordless Onboarding">
  <h1>Example: Invite, Set Password, Log In</h1>
  <p>The end-to-end onboarding flow: an admin invites a user without exposing self-serve signup, the user picks a password through an invitation link, and the system logs them straight in.</p>

  <h2>Step 1 — Admin invites the user</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/InviteUser \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "role": "member",
    "recovery_email": "newperson-backup@example.com",
    "create_immediately": false
  }'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": {
    "id": "user_01HXABCDE...",
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "role": "member",
    "status": "USER_STATUS_INVITED"
  },
  "invitationToken": "inv_e3a9c7...",
  "setupUrl": "https://app.example.com/accept-invite?token=inv_e3a9c7..."
}</code></pre>
  <p>The admin's frontend forwards <code>setupUrl</code> to the user via the email service (or copies it from the response and sends it manually). At this point the User node exists with <code>status=invited</code>; logins for that account are blocked until the invitation is accepted.</p>
  <p>Audit event written: <code>user_invited</code>.</p>

  <h2>Step 2 — User opens the link</h2>
  <p>The frontend at <code>https://app.example.com/accept-invite</code> reads the <code>token</code> query parameter and shows a "Set your password" form. On submit it calls <code>AcceptInvitation</code>:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/AcceptInvitation \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "invitation_token": "inv_e3a9c7...",
    "password": "Their5tronger#Pass",
    "name": "New Person"
  }'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": {
    "id": "user_01HXABCDE...",
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "status": "USER_STATUS_ACTIVE"
  },
  "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...",
  "refreshToken": "rt_...",
  "expiresIn": 900
}</code></pre>

  <Callout type="info" title="No double sign-in">
    <code>AcceptInvitation</code> is auth-exempt and returns a session immediately. There is no "set password" &rarr; "now log in" round-trip; the password is set and the session is issued atomically.
  </Callout>

  <p>Audit event written: <code>login_success</code> with <code>method=invitation</code> in the details JSON.</p>

  <h2>Step 3 — User explores</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/GetCurrentUser \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -d '{}'
# &rarr; { user: { ..., status: "USER_STATUS_ACTIVE" } }</code></pre>

  <h2>Optional — Add a passkey</h2>
  <p>To make the next login truly passwordless, the user can register a passkey while the invitation session is still fresh:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash"># 1. Begin
curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/BeginPasskeyRegistration \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -d '{"device_name":"My Laptop"}'
# &rarr; { optionsJson, challengeId }

# 2. Frontend calls navigator.credentials.create(options); then:
curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/CompletePasskeyRegistration \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -d '{"challenge_id":"pkc_...","credential_json":"<from navigator>","device_name":"My Laptop"}'</code></pre>
  <p>Audit event: <code>passkey_added</code>. From now on, the user can sign in with <code>BeginPasskeyLogin</code> + <code>CompletePasskeyLogin</code> &mdash; no password prompt at all.</p>

  <h2>What if the user doesn't accept?</h2>
  <p>The User node sits in <code>status=invited</code> indefinitely. The invitation token is single-use; if it leaks before acceptance, the admin can call <code>ResetUserPassword</code> with <code>generate_temp_password=false</code> to invalidate the old token and issue a fresh one (or call <code>DeleteUser</code> to roll the invitation back entirely).</p>

  <h2>Variant — Admin generates a temporary password</h2>
  <p>For offline onboarding (e.g. handing off credentials in person):</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST https://id.app.com/identity.IdentityService/InviteUser \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_ACCESS" \
  -d '{
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "role": "member",
    "create_immediately": true
  }'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": { "id": "user_...", "status": "USER_STATUS_ACTIVE" },
  "temporaryPassword": "Tmp-Z7q9wK7s5N..."
}</code></pre>
  <p>The user logs in with the temporary password and immediately calls <code>ChangePassword</code> to pick something they'll remember.</p>
</DocsLayout>
